      "writtenOn": "2022-03-03T20:46:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"build ID\" is just the value in build/make/core/build_id.mk, it\u0027s probably not what you want.  \"Build number\" is probably what you want, which you can get from using `$(cat)` in your command line to get the contents of ctx.Config().BuildNumberFile(ctx).\n\nWe don\u0027t have the name of the build server build, or the value of TARGET_BUILD_VARIANT.  You can reconstruct an approximation of TARGET_BUILD_VARIANT using `ctx.Config().Debuggable()` and `ctx.Config().Eng()`, but you won\u0027t be able to handle cases where the build server build has some extra suffix.",
      "parentUuid": "d728498c_75c1e451",
